{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Environment", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What Is the Ozone Layer?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe environmental change in social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Simple Past tense to talk about many kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, when you use the Simple Past tense, the time of the finished action is clear from the context or explicitly mentioned in the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">In the 1980s, scientists <span class=\"strong\">recognized </span>that human actions had a negative effect on the global ozone layer.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here, it is clear when the action of \u201crecognizing\u201d happened (in the 1980s) and that it finished in that time period. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here is another example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">However, in 1985, they <span class=\"strong\">discovered</span> a large hole in the ozone that is growing above Antarctica.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember that there are both regular and irregular verbs. Look at the chart for examples of the Simple Past tense verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Regular Verb</div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Irregular Verb</div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discover\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discovered\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"recognize\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"recognized\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"know\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"knew\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "In the 1980s, scientists recognized that human actions had a negative effect on the global ozone layer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "At first, scientists thought that the ozone layer was slowly thinning all over the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "However, in 1985, they discovered a large hole in the ozone that is growing above Antarctica.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">Few people actually know what exactly <span class=\"strong\">is happening</span> to the ozone layer.</span></p><p>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">Most of us <span class=\"strong\">have seen</span> products that claim to be \"ozone friendly\" or \"CFC free\u201d.</span></p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic and scientific writing. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">am</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">are</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">being </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">A thinner ozone layer means life on earth <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is being exposed</span> to too much ultraviolet radiation. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">has</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">been </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Damage to the ozone layer <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has been caused</span> by certain chemicals called CFCs.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Most of us have seen products that claim to be \"ozone friendly\" or \"CFC free,\" but few people actually know what exactly is happening to the ozone layer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Research has shown that damage to the ozone layer has been caused by certain chemicals called CFCs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Industries have used these chemicals in refrigeration, air conditioning, cleaning materials, and aerosol sprays for a long time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "However, in 1985, they discovered a large hole in the ozone that is growing above Antarctica.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Each year the ozone over this part of the earth has been reduced by over 50 percent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A thinner ozone layer means life on earth is being exposed to too much ultraviolet radiation. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ultraviolet ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cannot be seen by people, but responsible for making your skin darker in the sun", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The ozone layer protects the Earth from the Sun's ultraviolet rays. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about issues with the ozone layer:.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ray ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a beam of light", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Sun produces ultraviolet rays. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "life ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " living things, including plants, animals", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Without the ozone layer, no life could survive on the planet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "refrigeration ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the process of keeping items to cool", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Industries use CFCs in refrigeration. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "aerosol ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a substance kept under pressure and able to be released as a fine spray", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Industries have used these chemicals in refrigeration, air conditioning, cleaning materials, and aerosol sprays for a long time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "photosynthesis ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the process by which a green plant uses sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This interferes with plants' abilities to get energy through photosynthesis. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to interfere", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to prevent something happening", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "verb", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This interferes with plants' abilities to get energy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to eliminate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to completely get rid of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "verb", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many countries have tried to eliminate the manufacture and use of CFCs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch a movie about extreme environmental catastrophes, like <span class=\"italic\">Arctic Blast</span> or <span class=\"italic\">The Day After Tomorrow</span>.\t", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think about how that relates to what you've read about the ozone layer and the environment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss with a partner whether you think these movies are realistic or not.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch a movie about an extreme environmental catastrophe.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I reflect on what I've learned about the environment and how that relates to the movie.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the movie with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to manufacture", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make goods by machine, usually in large numbers or amounts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They manufacture books in factories.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob02aud09", "type": "audio"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can describe social and urban change, and environmental problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that happened.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that are happening and things that have happened. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How much do you know about the ozone layer? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What effect do chemicals in the air 