", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le02ob02re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Most of us have seen products that claim to be \"ozone friendly\" or \"CFC free,\" but few people actually know what exactly is happening to the ozone layer.<br/>\nThe ozone layer is a part of the earth's atmosphere (about 24 miles thick) that protects it from the sun's ultraviolet rays. Without the ozone layer, no life could survive on the planet. In the 1980s, scientists recognized that human actions had a negative effect on the global ozone layer."}, {"time": "29000", "image": "engenn9le02ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Research has shown that damage to the ozone layer has been caused by certain chemicals called CFCs (chlorofluorocarbons).<br/>\nIndustries have used these chemicals in refrigeration, air conditioning, cleaning materials, and aerosol sprays for a long time.<br/>\nAt first, scientists thought that the ozone layer was slowly thinning all over the world. However, in 1985, they discovered a large hole in the ozone that is growing above Antarctica."}, {"time": "59000", "image": "engenn9le02ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Each year the ozone over this part of the earth has been reduced by over 50 percent. A thinner ozone layer means life on earth is being exposed to too much ultraviolet radiation. This can cause skin cancer, make the immune system less effective, and interfere with plants' abilities to get energy through photosynthesis. Ocean plants are also being threatened.<br/>\nMany countries have tried to eliminate the manufacture and use of CFCs. However, CFCs can stay in the atmosphere for more than 100 years - a concern that will remain for a century to come."}]}}], "_data": [], "id": 1, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena"}